.TH CTBREC-WEBUI-PATCH 1 "2026-11-09" "ctbrec-webui-patch" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-webui-patch \- add a fetch-portrait button to the ctbrec web interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-webui-patch
[\fBapply\fP|\fBrevert\fP|\fBstatus\fP]
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-webui-patch
installs a small override of the ctbrec web interface that adds a
.B "Fetch from stream"
button to the portrait popup. The button asks the running server to download
the model's current preview, save it as the portrait, and show it in the
popup immediately. On Stripchat this is a frame from the newest recording, not
the static site preview or the default profile avatar; the server converts it
to JPEG so both the browser and the desktop client can display it. This
requires the companion
.BR ImageServlet
patch (see
.I ~/.local/share/ctbrec/README.md
for that patch).
.P
This is the same operation as clicking the portrait box in
the Edit Model dialog, but reachable from the portrait viewer itself.
.P
ctbrec serves its web interface from resources inside the server jar. Its
launcher puts
.I /opt/ctbrec/patch
first on the classpath, and the static file servlet resolves resources through
the class loader, so a file placed at
.I /opt/ctbrec/patch/html/static/index.html
or
.I models.js
silently overrides the jar copy. No jar modification and no server restart is
needed; a normal browser reload picks it up.
.P
The script extracts the pristine files from the installed jar, checks that the
patch anchors are present and unique, applies the changes, verifies the
JavaScript syntax with
.BR node (1)
when available, pushes the files through
.BR pct (1)
and makes them owned by the
.B ctbrec
user.
.P
Because the override survives package changes, re-run
.B ctbrec-webui-patch apply
after every ctbrec upgrade. If an upgrade changes the relevant markup or
JavaScript, the anchor check fails and nothing is deployed; use
.B status
or
.B revert
to inspect or remove a stale override.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B apply
Extract, patch and deploy the two override files. This is the default action.
Safe to repeat.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the deployed override files carry the patch marker. Exits 0 when
both are patched, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B revert
Remove the two override files if (and only if) they carry the patch marker,
restoring the stock web interface. Other files under the patch directory are
left untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server " HOST"
SSH host running the ctbrec container. Default:
.BR proxmox ,
overridable with
.BR CTBREC_WEBUI_SERVER .
.TP
.B \-\-vmid " ID"
Proxmox container ID. Default:
.BR 109 ,
overridable with
.BR CTBREC_WEBUI_VMID .
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-dir " PATH"
ctbrec installation directory inside the container. Default:
.BR /opt/ctbrec ,
overridable with
.BR CTBREC_WEBUI_DIR .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Find the jar and verify the anchors without deploying anything.
.SH WHAT CHANGES
.IP \(bu 2
.I index.html
gains a footer in the portrait popup containing the button, and the
.I models.js
script tag gets a version query so browsers pick up the new file.
.IP \(bu 2
.I models.js
gains a global holding the popup's model URL and a
.B fetchPortraitForPopup()
function which calls
.B ../image/portrait/fetch/<url>
and refreshes the image, with a spinner and a notification.
.IP \(bu 2
Every inserted line carries a
.B ctbrec-webui-patch
marker, which is how
.B status
and
.B revert
recognise the overrides.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install or refresh the button:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-webui-patch apply
.EE
.P
Check that it is deployed:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-webui-patch status
.EE
.P
Validate anchors before a real run:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-webui-patch apply \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Return to the stock web interface:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-webui-patch revert
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for
.B status
this means the override is present.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: no jar found, anchor missing or duplicated, remote command failed, or
(for
.B status
) the override is absent.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/ctbrec/patch/html/static/index.html
Patched page override.
.TP
.I /opt/ctbrec/patch/html/static/models.js
Patched script override.
.TP
.I /opt/ctbrec/ctbrec-server-*-final.jar
Pristine source of both files; never modified.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits (1),
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR pct (1)
.SH NOTES
After deploying, hard-refresh the browser
(for example with
.BR Ctrl+Shift+R )
if the old
.I models.js
is still cached. The stock image popup is otherwise unchanged: the camera
button only appears in the portrait dialog.
